But here >>

The kernel is a Python process running in the background.
When you run a cell, it sends the code to the kernel, which executes it and sends back the result.
All cells share the same kernel, so variables persist between cells.


Notebook UI      Kernel                Keeps variables in memory
                Python process         Runs cells in whatever order you click
                                       Dies when you restart it

